How many applicants scored **more than $40$**?

The ogive shows the results of $100$ runners in a $10\text{ km}$ race.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,6.0);
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (6.5,0);
\foreach \y in {20,40,60,80,100} {\draw (-0.15,\y/20) -- (0,\y/20); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,\y/20) {$\y$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.15,0) {$0$};
\foreach \x/\val in {1/30,2/40,3/50,4/60,5/70} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\val$};}
\draw[thick] (0,0) -- (1,0.2) -- (2,0.6) -- (3,2.5) -- (4,4.4) -- (5,5.0);
\foreach \p in {(0,0),(1,0.2),(2,0.6),(3,2.5),(4,4.4),(5,5.0)} {\fill \p circle (2.5pt);}
\node[rotate=90] at (-1.3,2.5) {Cumulative frequency};
\node[below] at (2.5,-1.0) {Time (minutes)};
\node at (2.5,5.7) {Race finish times};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which statement correctly gives the estimated median and interquartile range ($IQR$) if $Q_1 \approx 43.5\text{ min}$ and $Q_3 \approx 56.5\text{ min}$?
